{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Vanessa Starts Dating Marco", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Chocolate, Anyone? ", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 9, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 9, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe characteristics of different people and their jobs.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "The First Conditional", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You can use the first conditional to talk about actions and situations in the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "There are two parts to the sentence. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "One part is the <span class=\"strong\">condition.</span> The other part is the <span class=\"strong\">result</span> .", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Form:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">If</span> + <span class=\"italic\">subject</span> + <span class=\"italic\">Simple Present tense</span>  + <span class=\"italic\">subject</span> + <span class=\"italic\">will/may/might</span> <br> You use a comma after the condition in this form. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Condition\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Result\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If you want to find out,</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">you'll have to come back tomorrow.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "You can change the two parts of the sentence so that the result comes first.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Result\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Condition\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I might believe you </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">if you show me what's inside.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Quantifiers", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use a quantifier before a noun to indicate the amount or number of an item.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use quantifiers with both count and non-count nouns.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use all of the quantifiers below with both count and non-count nouns.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Quantifier\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"more<br> less/fewer <br>no/none<br> any/not any<br>  some <br> a lot of/lots of<br>plenty of<br> enough\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a larger number/amount <br> a smaller number/amount<br>  0, nothing<br> ask about a number or amount/say there is no<br>  a small number/amount<br>  a very large number/amount<br>  more than you need<br>  as much as you need\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Did you buy enough groceries?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I don't see any eggs in here.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I may buy more bread.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "veal", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the meat from a young cow ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I like eating veal more than chicken.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob09aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about about food and drinks.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "marsala ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "cooked with a sweet strong wine ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I made you some veal marsala.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "milk ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a white liquid from cows or goats that people drink ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If it's too spicy, drink some milk.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "chocolate chip ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "small pieces of chocolate ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I like chocolate chip cookies.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "oatmeal ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "crushed oats used in baking or cooking", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This cookie is made from oatmeal. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "raisin ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a dried grape ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I put raisins in the cookie dough too.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to spoil ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to look after someone in a way that is very kind ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He spoiled me with all these home-cooked meals.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob09aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "caramel ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a sticky brown sweet made of sugar, butter, and milk ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I bought you a box of caramels. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Who is your favorite celebrity (famous person)?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Imagine you have to cook a meal for them. What would you make? Why?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down the ingredients you need to make this meal.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "What would you give them to drink?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a short paragraph using your answers. Start your topic sentence with <span class=\"italic\">If I cook a meal for my favorite celebrity, I will make them ...</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Proofread your paragraph.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice reading it aloud.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I write about food.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about events in the future.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about food.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "engenn5le09ob09re2aud01", "images": [{"image": "engenn5le09ob09re2img07.jpg", "id": 0, "time": "0", "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn5le09ob09re2img07.jpg", "id": 1, "time": "100", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Marco! What are you doing here?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Marco</span>: If I say I was in the area, will you believe me?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I might believe you if you show me what's inside your bag.<br>"}, {"image": "engenn5le09ob09re2img07.jpg", "id": 2, "time": "11000", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Marco</span>: When you invite me in, I may show you.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Sorry, come in!<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Marco</span>: Thanks."}, {"image": "engenn5le09ob09re2img06.jpg", "id": 3, "time": "19000", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Did you go grocery shopping? It looks like you got plenty of groceries.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Marco</span>: No ... but I have something for you.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: For me? <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Marco</span>: Yeah, remember when I said I'd cook for you? I made you veal marsala. <br>"}, {"image": "engenn5le09ob09re2img06.jpg", "id": 4, "time": "33000", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Aw, Marco! <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Marco</span>: Before you try it, you'll have to get some milk. It's spicy! I made you my famous chocolate chip oatmeal raisin cookies too. I think there might be fewer chocolate chips than raisins though. Sorry.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: You're spoiling me! I definitely think there are enough chocolate chips in here. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Marco</span>: Good. I had a box of caramels too, but I ate them on the way over."}], "coverimg": "engenn5le09ob09re2img07.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "I can talk about food and drinks.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can use words to describe general quantities.  ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can talk about hypothetical actions and events in the future.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "Do you ever surprise your friends? What did you do?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "Do you cook for your friends?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_fee